  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Papua New Guinea Sustainable Landscapes Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Papua New Guinea):  USAID, through the Papua New Guinea Sustainable Landscapes (PNGSL) activity, will bolster PNG&apos;s ongoing efforts to reduce greenhouse gas (GHG) emissions, enhance carbon sequestration, and address COVID-19 impacts through technical assistance and training that will increase capture of its forests&apos; value and align economic development policies and incentives with natural resource conservation to benefit local communities. Interventions will seek the following objectives:.Strengthen land and natural resources governance - Through the work of PNGSL, USAID will improve the implementation of safeguards for infrastructure development; enhance the vertical and horizontal integration of participatory low-emission land use planning; and protect high carbon-density areas.  .Improve the environmental sustainability of the forestry industry - USAID will increase adherence to social and environmental safeguards by forestry companies; improve implementation and coordination of sustainable forestry policies; and build capacity to enforce sustainable forestry policies.  .Protect the natural resource management rights of communities - USAID will increase the capacity of rural communities to protect land and forest resource rights; improve the financial literacy and business acumen of forest owners; and enhance the transparency and integrity of information on natural resources..Strengthening natural resource governance advances the vision for an open, interconnected, resilient, and secure Indo-Pacific by protecting and advancing the region&apos;s rules-based order. Promoting transparent government policies, regulations, and transactions fosters adherence to internationally accepted standards, including environmental safeguards, and mitigates the entry and actions of predatory players.</narrative>
  </description>
